    <string name="section_about">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="privacy_statement_body">Stream Anything collects nothing and has no backend of its own. There\'s no analytics, and the links you play are only sent to the site hosting the video, to fetch and stream it. To let you resume, it remembers where you stopped in your last 50 videos as unreadable fingerprints — not links or titles — unless you turn on Show History, which saves the links so it can list them. Either way it stays on this device, never uploaded or backed up, and you can turn it off or clear it under Playback. Play on TV, if you turn it on, only talks to your own paired devices on your Wi-Fi: links go straight between your phone and your TV, never through the internet.</string>
    <string name="content_disclaimer_body">Stream Anything doesn\'t host, index, or provide any videos. It only plays links you supply — you\'re responsible for having the right to watch them.</string>
